  "rules": {
    "analysis": "Early windows exercise boundary distinctions and share source group with full packet. Two #690 controls share a related cluster. All are development. Report task, strict alive/composite, linked alive/composite and uncertainty separately.",
    "exploratory_alive": "A named identity view and living endpoint linked through the same session and exact operation interval with no observed identity change. Attend to whether the endpoint shows living gameplay or active survivor menu rather than save/title/death. Attribute unknown on any unresolved linkage.",
    "strict_alive": "Named same survivor and visible living state at the assigned endpoint. A named death makes the composite negative, leaving task separate. Title/load/exit is an unknown living endpoint.",
    "task": "Acquisition of a usable ration in the assigned interval followed by observed consumption of that acquired stock and a visible change. Track baseline, carried, nearby and selected stock separately. Show absence or incompletion at baseline. Score unknown for missing comparability or unresolved acquisition/use; show boundary for early/partial episodes. A positive in the composite requires alive."
  },
